    "\"The doc's a secondary source — the last session wrote down what it believed, not what's true. Have the new session run the auth tests and trust the primary source.\"": "“文档只是二手来源——上一次会话写下的是它当时相信的内容，不一定是真实情况。让新会话运行认证测试，并相信一手来源。”",
    "\"The handoff doc says auth is done, but the new session keeps finding broken token refresh.\"": "“交接文档说认证已经完成，但新会话一直发现 Token 刷新存在问题。”",
    "A lot of context engineering is the manufacture of secondary sources. Compaction turns the session history into a summary that seeds the next session. A subagent burns its own context on a noisy search and returns a short report. A handoff artifact condenses a session's decisions into a document the next session reads. Memory systems distil what a session learned into notes. Each makes the same trade: fidelity for headroom.": "大量<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context\">上下文</a>工程工作，其实都在制造二手来源。<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/compaction\">压缩</a>把<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a>历史变成摘要，为下一次会话提供起点；<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/subagent\">子智能体</a>用自己的上下文处理嘈杂搜索，再返回简短报告；<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/handoff-artifact\">交接产物</a>把会话决策浓缩成供下一次会话读取的文档；<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/memory-system\">记忆系统</a>把会话学到的内容提炼成笔记。它们都在做相同权衡：用保真度换取可用空间。",
    "An account of a primary source, one step removed — documentation describing code, a summary describing a transcript, a report describing search results. Cheaper to load into the context window than the source it describes, and lossy by construction: whoever wrote it decided what mattered, and whatever they dropped is invisible to a reader who only has the summary.": "二手来源是对<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/primary-source\">一手来源</a>的转述，中间隔了一层——例如描述代码的文档、概括对话记录的摘要、整理搜索结果的报告。把它加载进<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-window\">上下文窗口</a>，比加载原始来源更便宜；但它在结构上必然有损：写作者决定哪些内容重要，而任何被省略的信息，对只拿到摘要的读者都不可见。",
    "Neither failure makes secondary sources a mistake. The context window is finite, and primary sources are expensive; without summaries, reports, and handoff documents, nothing large fits. The skill is knowing which details can survive the loss — and verifying against the primary source when one can't. A well-made secondary source carries a context pointer back to its original — the summary that names the transcript it came from, the doc that names the file it describes — so when the account isn't enough, the reader can follow the pointer rather than work from the loss.": "这两类失败都不意味着二手来源本身是错误选择。上下文窗口容量有限，一手来源加载成本高；如果没有摘要、报告和交接文档，任何大型工作都装不进去。真正需要掌握的是：哪些细节可以承受损失，哪些不行时必须回到一手来源验证。优秀的二手来源会携带指向原始材料的<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/context-pointer\">上下文指针</a>——摘要注明自己来自哪段对话，文档注明自己描述哪个文件。这样，当转述不足时，读者可以沿指针读取原始内容，而不是被迫在缺失信息上继续工作。",
    "Secondary sources fail in two ways. They're lossy — the compaction summary that lost the schema decision, the report that didn't mention the edge case. And they drift — the primary source changes and the account doesn't follow, so docs describe last quarter's architecture with this quarter's confidence. When an agent acts on a secondary source that has failed either way, it works confidently from wrong information; the fix is sending it back to the primary source.": "二手来源会以两种方式失效。第一种是信息损失——压缩摘要漏掉了 schema 决策，报告没有提到边界情况。第二种是发生漂移——一手来源已经变化，转述却没有同步，于是文档用本季度的自信描述上季度的架构。当<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>依据任一种失效的二手来源行动时，就会自信地使用错误信息；解决办法是让它回到一手来源。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>"
